The task is to push a new build of an edge function (a Worker) and make it live. This could involve uploading a version and then deploying it. The workers-versions group covers uploading code as a version, but going live requires a deployment, which is in workers-deployments. The wrangler skill would handle both in one step (`wrangler deploy`), but it only applies if the project has a wrangler config file, which the task doesn't say.

The workers-legacy group, which uploads a script in one step, is another candidate. The task says "push a new build... and make it live," which suggests an upload-and-deploy flow. Workers-versions is the natural starting point because it handles uploading new code, and its description points to deployments as the next step.

